# Build context for the importer image (Issue #224). The Dockerfile copies
# requirements.txt, poll.py and lookups.py by name, so nothing else needs to
# reach the daemon — and parsers/ specifically must not: it is gitignored,
# user-specific,
# and encodes how someone categorizes their own transactions. Keeping it out of
# the context keeps it out of the build cache as well as the image.
parsers/

# The test suite and its dependencies are build-time-only (#124). The Dockerfile
# copies its sources by name so these would not reach the image
# regardless, but keeping them out of the context keeps them out of the build
# cache too — and stops a pytest pin from looking like a runtime dependency.
tests/
requirements-dev.txt

__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

Dockerfile
.dockerignore
